<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  AI feeds for newsletter4link, every one fetched and checked on 4 August 2026.

  Each feed here returned HTTP 200, parsed as RSS or Atom, contained at least one
  item, and had published something within the previous 60 days. Feeds that only
  parse are not enough: the public "awesome AI feeds" OPML lists are full of
  sources that still serve XML from 2018.

  Excluded on purpose, having been tested and found unusable: Anthropic, Mistral
  and Meta AI publish no RSS at all (404 on every documented path); The Batch,
  Stanford HAI, LangChain and Modal return a page with no items; SemiAnalysis
  last published 322 days ago.

  Also excluded because you already have them active: OpenAI and Google AI Blog.

  The importer reads the folder name as the category, so importing this once
  categorises every feed correctly. Leave the category field in the dialog alone.

  READ THIS BEFORE ENABLING THE AI Preprints GROUP. Those four arXiv feeds carry
  100 to 710 items each, per day, and curation makes four Claude calls per
  article. Switching all four on multiplies the cost of a run by roughly two
  hundred. They are in their own group so they can be imported without being
  enabled, and they want a much higher relevance threshold than the rest. arXiv
  publishes Sunday to Thursday: an empty feed on Friday and Saturday is by design,
  not a fault.

  Two notes on the community entries. Anthropic publishes no RSS at all, so its
  entry is a community mirror that has to be re-checked monthly: the failure mode
  is silent staleness, not an error. Reddit throttles hard, and returned HTTP 429
  on a single request for r/MachineLearning and r/ClaudeAI, so only r/LocalLLaMA
  is included and it should be polled no more than hourly.

  Corrections to the source research, all found by fetching: the MCP blog serves
  no feed at /rss or /feed, only at /index.xml; SemiAnalysis last published 322
  days ago and is not a live source; rss.sapo.pt/tek/ does not resolve at all.
-->
